# AI-Agent-Talkshow — project rules

## Language

- **All git-tracked files must be in English** (README, ROADMAP, CONTRIBUTING, YAML comments, new code comments).
- Do not add Chinese to files that will be pushed to GitHub.

## Before coding

1. Read [ROADMAP.md](../../ROADMAP.md) for priorities.
2. Read [README.md](../../README.md) for setup and architecture.
3. Read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../../CONTRIBUTING.md) for workflow.

## Architecture constraints

- **Single LiveKit agent participant** with role handoff — do not spawn 3 separate RTC agents without explicit design approval.
- **Shared `show_history`** — panelists share one transcript; disambiguate roles in prompts (Human guest ≠ Amy).
- **Gemma calls:** `complete_from_wav` (human audio) and `complete_text` (panel lines); `StoredReplyLLM` does not call the model again.

## Current roadmap (Phase 2+)

1. Debate scenario + few-shot examples
2. Host-moderated turn-taking (hand-raise or host picks speaker from history)
3. Avatar expressions/motion in `talkshow-web`

Implement against ROADMAP checklists; update ROADMAP when items ship.

## Dev split

- **Babel:** agent worker, vLLM, Piper
- **Laptop:** `talkshow-web`, `api/tokens.py`
- Agent sync: `./scripts/sync-to-babel.sh` (local, not in repo)

## Code style

- Minimal diff; match existing patterns in `agent/` and `talkshow-web/`.
- No commits unless the user explicitly asks.
